  "notes": "The jazz-trained multi-instrumentalist end of this lane, and the one board entry here whose harmony is the researched fact rather than an inference. The research is explicit: he \"studied jazz piano at The New School under Jaki Byard\", and \"expect major-7ths, 9ths, inverted bass, chromatic passing chords and modal borrowing where a peer would use plain triads\". So `triad` sits at 0.22 — the lowest in this section — with `seventh` and `ninth` carrying the rest, `susOrDimProb` covering the chromatic passing chords, and a ii—V—I family beside the pop ones; \"loops are 4 or 8 bars with a genuine harmonic move rather than a vamp\" is why `vamp` is absent from `harmonicRhythm` altogether, which no other model in this batch does. The drums are played by him: \"dry, tightly tuned, mid-forward backbeat with minimal reverb, plus handclaps and tambourine. He engineers and programs his own sessions, so drum sounds are chosen at source rather than replaced.\" That is a short-reverb medium-transient snare, a loose humanize block, `tambourine` percs, and no roll vocabulary at all. The bass is the second signature: \"he plays the bass — fingered electric or analogue synth — usually a melodic line that moves against a static kick rather than doubling it\", so the kick stays square while the bassline is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.24, the lowest here, with a full passing-tone set. No `bass808` block: the entry says \"no 808\". \"Bossa-and-Beach-Boys-informed voicings\" is the `close` voicing and the arch melody; the counter is the keyboard or guitar figure. Arrangement authors \"a real bridge with a key or modal shift\" as a full bridge slot and a higher `switchUpProb`. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every drum probability, the humanize numbers and `bpm.mode` 100 (the research gives 70—130 \"depending on artist\" with no centre, so the mode is that band's midpoint).",
